WEBVTT

00:00.621 --> 00:02.250
Five accounts say buy.

00:02.400 --> 00:03.990
Is that five opinions?

00:04.126 --> 00:06.992
Or one opinion, copied four times?

00:07.457 --> 00:09.369
Most trading bots can't tell the

00:09.119 --> 00:10.001
difference.

00:10.176 --> 00:11.547
They count the noise,

00:11.684 --> 00:13.493
act on it, and keep no

00:13.256 --> 00:14.343
record of why.

00:14.764 --> 00:15.929
This is Hanko.

00:16.092 --> 00:17.746
A hanko is the seal you

00:17.496 --> 00:19.435
stamp in Japan to commit to

00:19.197 --> 00:20.027
something.

00:20.190 --> 00:22.527
Every decision here is stamped before

00:22.290 --> 00:23.636
the outcome is known.

00:24.077 --> 00:26.428
It reads public voices on Telegram,

00:26.603 --> 00:28.309
Bluesky and X.

00:28.446 --> 00:30.333
A repost, a forward,

00:30.495 --> 00:31.995
or a copy with an ad

00:31.758 --> 00:34.263
pasted on counts as one voice.

00:34.387 --> 00:35.345
Not two.

00:35.764 --> 00:37.071
Then it decides.

00:37.208 --> 00:39.404
Enter, pass, or admit it can't

00:39.167 --> 00:39.816
tell.

00:39.965 --> 00:41.478
It sizes the position,

00:41.383 --> 00:43.669
and writes down in advance exactly

00:43.432 --> 00:44.880
what would prove it wrong.

00:45.324 --> 00:47.507
Every run is sealed and anchored

00:47.321 --> 00:48.705
in a Bitcoin block.

00:48.880 --> 00:50.638
Change one byte, and the seal

00:50.388 --> 00:51.141
breaks.

00:51.264 --> 00:52.519
Anyone can check it,

00:52.463 --> 00:54.620
with no account and no key.

00:55.077 --> 00:57.106
Before it buys, it checks it

00:56.869 --> 00:57.750
can sell.

00:57.912 --> 01:00.198
Selling fifty thousand dollars of BONK

00:59.961 --> 01:01.861
costs under three percent,

01:02.010 --> 01:03.317
from a real quote.

01:03.454 --> 01:05.959
The textbook formula said seven point

01:05.709 --> 01:06.474
six.

01:06.911 --> 01:08.797
So we broke it on purpose.

01:08.934 --> 01:10.125
Sources down.

01:10.234 --> 01:11.399
Rate limits.

01:11.563 --> 01:13.114
A planted instruction.

01:13.264 --> 01:14.789
Tampered evidence.

01:14.952 --> 01:16.259
Nine failures.

01:16.369 --> 01:17.418
Nine held.

01:17.890 --> 01:20.176
And it runs every three hours,

01:20.120 --> 01:22.225
on its own, in public.

01:22.388 --> 01:24.957
Three days later, every call is

01:24.707 --> 01:26.864
graded against the conditions it set

01:26.627 --> 01:27.444
itself.

01:27.890 --> 01:28.681
Hanko.

01:28.831 --> 01:30.112
Don't trust the call.

01:30.261 --> 01:31.413
Check the receipt.
